tlv320adc3xxx: take the bit clock directly when it is the clock source

A device fed from the bit clock on a shared TDM bus does not need its PLL:
the bit clock already divides down to the sample rate, so the PLL divides by
one and contributes only jitter. Only the device generating the clock needs
one. The driver always routed CODEC_CLKIN through the PLL, so consumers paid
for jitter they had no use for.

Point CODEC_CLKIN at the bit clock instead when that is the source.

Measured on an Echo Dot 2nd gen microphone array, four TLV320ADC3101 on one
bus. Switching the three consumers part-way through a SINGLE capture, so the
room cannot account for it, dropped their 3-7 kHz noise floor by 14 to
19.5 dB while the producer, which keeps its PLL, moved 0.2 dB. The vendor
firmware clocks its consumers the same way (CLKGEN_MUX 0x01).

The PLL is deliberately left configured and powered rather than shut down.
Taking the driver's existing no-PLL path - a pll_p = 0 divider entry plus
ADC3XXX_NO_PLL - was tried and corrupts the SECOND ADC channel of every
device on the bus, left channels reading -65 dBFS while right channels read
-17 dBFS with full-scale spikes, even though every analogue register matched
the vendor byte for byte. Only the mux value is changed here.

--- a/sound/soc/codecs/tlv320adc3xxx.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/tlv320adc3xxx.c
@@ -282,6 +282,8 @@
 			 (ADC3XXX_CODEC_CLKIN_MCLK << ADC3XXX_CODEC_CLKIN_SHIFT))
 #define ADC3XXX_USE_PLL_BCLK	((ADC3XXX_PLL_CLKIN_BCLK << ADC3XXX_PLL_CLKIN_SHIFT) | \
 				 (ADC3XXX_CODEC_CLKIN_PLL_CLK << ADC3XXX_CODEC_CLKIN_SHIFT))
+#define ADC3XXX_NO_PLL_BCLK	((ADC3XXX_PLL_CLKIN_MCLK << ADC3XXX_PLL_CLKIN_SHIFT) | \
+				 (ADC3XXX_CODEC_CLKIN_BCLK << ADC3XXX_CODEC_CLKIN_SHIFT))
 
 /*  Analog PGA control bits */
 #define ADC3XXX_LPGA_MUTE		0x80
@@ -1300,8 +1302,21 @@
 	if (adc3xxx_divs[i].pll_p) { /* If PLL used for this mode */
 		adc3xxx_setup_pll(component, i);
 		snd_soc_component_write(component, ADC3XXX_CLKGEN_MUX,
+					/*
+					 * A device fed from the bit clock takes it DIRECTLY. Its
+					 * PLL would divide by one and contribute only jitter:
+					 * measured on a four device array, routing the three
+					 * consumers through the PLL costs 14 to 19.5 dB of
+					 * 3-7 kHz noise floor, while the producer, which needs
+					 * its PLL to make the clock, is unaffected.
+					 *
+					 * The PLL is left configured and powered rather than
+					 * shut down. Taking the driver's full no-PLL path here
+					 * corrupts the second ADC channel of every device, and
+					 * this is the arrangement that was verified working.
+					 */
 					adc3xxx->pll_clkin == ADC3XXX_PLL_CLKIN_BCLK ?
-					ADC3XXX_USE_PLL_BCLK : ADC3XXX_USE_PLL);
+					ADC3XXX_NO_PLL_BCLK : ADC3XXX_USE_PLL);
 		if (!adc3xxx->use_pll) {
 			snd_soc_dapm_add_routes(dapm, adc3xxx_pll_intercon,
 						ARRAY_SIZE(adc3xxx_pll_intercon));
